<hr>
<h1 id="hudhud-fm-execution-plan-cohesive-batches-with-independent-evidence">HudHud FM execution plan — cohesive batches with independent evidence</h1>
<h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Authorized implementation in progress. R01–R13 remain OPEN.</strong> The original planning baseline is retained below for audit. Current implementation, actual results and unresolved gates are tracked in [execution-progress.md](execution-progress.md); source/test changes are authorized, while production operations remain separate.</li><li>Preserve all <strong>65 atomic task IDs</strong>: <strong>54 source/test/contract tasks in 16 implementation batches</strong>, plus <strong>11 independent review, QA, device, rehearsal and operational tasks</strong>. Original task acceptance criteria remain mandatory.</li><li>Preserve all <strong>17 registered verification waves</strong> in [waves.json](waves.json), separate from work-assignment batches. Consolidation does not reduce testing or bypass gates.</li><li>B15 colocates comment-count authority, harness integration, privacy QA and pagination QA. This removes the cycle where WO-03 acceptance waits for a worker that itself waits for WO-03 acceptance.</li><li>Integration owner <strong>I</strong> owns cross-batch/control paths; designated component owners retain intrabatch content writes. Stable component workers reuse context; parallel execution requires disjoint writes and runtime resources, not merely different WO labels.</li></ul>
<h2 id="current-execution-snapshot">Current execution snapshot</h2>
<p>B15 scoped native 125/125 and B16 T10/T11 reviewed source handoffs are integrated; T11 root 64/64, Functions 413/413 and lint pass. T12 actual Rules guards pass 78/78; native notification/migration/seal/lease/ACK/query/index fixture remains preparing/unrun. Actual admin runtime passes 43/43 and independent mapping verifies all original 17 plus eight additional ordinary skipped identities on this candidate; ordinary admin 115/25 skips remain honestly separate. Public 83, frontend lint/build, Flutter 397/analyze/format, Android/iOS simulator debug builds, post-public-build Functions 413 and governance pass within recorded scope. All findings remain OPEN. Final native/changed-candidate/independent QA, browser (Debugger unattached) and physical Android/iPhone (0/0, NOT RUN) gates remain; production operations are separately unauthorized. Historical RED/failure/skip records and all task/wave/checkpoint states remain unchanged; see execution-progress.md and independent review/provenance for exact hashes and limits.</p>
<h2 id="document-information">Document information</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Project</td><td><code>hudhud_fm</code> only; excludes <code>FM-Pro</code></td></tr><tr><td>Original planning date / baseline</td><td>2026-10-25 / <code>9fae3248aadecaa53198a5fb9f06576fdcc182cf</code>; authorized continuation resumed at <code>c304e85</code></td></tr><tr><td>Current branch / local default</td><td><code>hudhud_fm</code> / <code>origin/main</code></td></tr><tr><td>Inputs</td><td>[Review](tech-review.md), [WO-01](WO-01.md), [WO-02](WO-02.md), [WO-03](WO-03.md), [WO-04](WO-04.md), previous master and [waves.json](waves.json)</td></tr><tr><td>Scheduling authority</td><td>This master and consolidated batches govern coordination; WOs retain exact task write sets and acceptance criteria</td></tr><tr><td>Execution authority</td><td>User authorized all four Work Orders and the S01 platform-link supplement. Execute dependency-ordered batches with RED/GREEN and independent review; production data, migrations, deployment and protected merges remain unauthorized</td></tr><tr><td>Language</td><td>English throughout, including artifacts, instructions, progress and final summaries</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="0-original-planning-preflight-historical">0. Original planning preflight — historical</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Observation / action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Git at planning baseline</td><td>The original planning preflight recorded no tracked source change. Authorized implementation later modified source/tests; refresh HEAD and worktree before each dispatch</td></tr><tr><td>Node at planning baseline</td><td>PATH was <code>v26.6.0</code>; execution uses the validated Node22.23.3 path. Refresh the toolchain before Node gates; no implicit installation</td></tr><tr><td>Dependencies</td><td>npm lockfiles exist; no dependency upgrade, lockfile edit or package installation planned</td></tr><tr><td>CI</td><td>No configuration found in inspected <code>.github/workflows</code>, <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code>, <code>.circleci</code>, Vercel/Netlify locations. Hosted CI commands remain <strong>UNKNOWN</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Verification authority</td><td>Actual package scripts and quality contract; do not invent an admin typecheck script or CI pass</td></tr><tr><td>Architecture</td><td>Riverpod, <code>presentation -&gt; domain &lt;- data</code>, one player; retain React/Firebase component boundaries</td></tr><tr><td>Historical evidence</td><td>368 passed, 17 skipped, three expected failing temporary reproductions; historical review evidence, not results of this plan</td></tr><tr><td>R13 planning decision gap</td><td>The original fixed-Yemen/accepted-offset disagreement was resolved by the approved per-schedule-offset policy and ADR. R13 remains OPEN; B16 source implementation and its receipt/cutover gates have not started</td></tr><tr><td>Devices</td><td>[Existing worksheet](../../docs/release/november-2026-device-acceptance.md) is NOT RUN; simulator/builds do not substitute</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Before every dispatch, check HEAD, exact write set, owner, contracts, worker availability and locks. Unknown paths/owners or unlisted writes block dispatch until the plan is updated. Preflight does not require reading secrets or private Firebase configuration.</p>
<h3 id="english-only-artifact-rendering">English-only artifact rendering</h3>
<p>All new documents, handoffs and reports remain English. Use <code>--lang en</code> on Boss commands that advertise that option. The installed runtime artifact/status commands do not expose a language flag; <code>.boss/templates/artifact.html.template</code> supplies English-only companion rendering without changing the installed skill or application. The original technical review remains an unchanged historical input.</p>
<h2 id="1-scope-and-acceptance">1. Scope and acceptance</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Source work order</th><th>Exact findings</th><th>Required outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>WO-01</td><td>R01, R10</td><td>Separate private station data; close all profile-email producers/consumers while preserving Auth and verification</td></tr><tr><td>WO-02</td><td>R02, R03, R05</td><td>Correct visible timer, safe replay, accurate dispatch result without duplicate accounts</td></tr><tr><td>WO-03</td><td>R04, R06, R07, R08</td><td>Bounded pages with complete reachability, safe counts, correct exports and bounded public archives</td></tr><tr><td>WO-04</td><td>R09, R11, R12, R13</td><td>Correct XML, fair health progress, one idempotent count authority, compatible timing/receipts</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Finding lifecycle: <code>OPEN -&gt; IN_PROGRESS -&gt; IMPLEMENTED -&gt; VERIFIED -&gt; CLOSED</code>. A plan does not advance status. Closure requires the fix, permanent regression, independent review and applicable gates. Missing device/operational evidence still blocks release approval even after local code is complete.</p>
<h2 id="2-stable-workers-and-physical-write-ownership">2. Stable workers and physical-write ownership</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Stable role</th><th>Assignment policy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>I</td><td>Delivery / Integration Lead</td><td>Coordination and sole content writer for cross-batch/control paths; merges approved batch commits without independent content edits; cannot approve its own implementation</td></tr><tr><td>BE</td><td>Backend</td><td>Server modules and designated intrabatch paths; prepares cross-batch/control patches for I</td></tr><tr><td>DT</td><td>Data Tools</td><td>Audit/repair/restore tools and synthetic fixtures, including designated intrabatch paths</td></tr><tr><td>FL</td><td>Flutter</td><td>Reuses context across B07, B08 and B09; this default capacity order is not a new functional DAG edge</td></tr><tr><td>WA</td><td>Web Admin</td><td>Forms, queries and export; consults BE for aggregate-server changes without overlapping write authority</td></tr><tr><td>WP</td><td>Public Web</td><td>Content repository and bounded archive UI</td></tr><tr><td>QA</td><td>Independent QA</td><td>Integration regressions/evidence; cannot approve application code it implemented</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Default capacity is one coordinator and at most three implementation workers, with one available worker per role code. Adding another FL worker requires a distinct identity, isolated worktree/build cache and disjoint writes. Multiple sessions do not automatically isolate files or emulators.</p>
<h3 id="2-1-single-integration-owner-registry">2.1 Single integration-owner registry</h3>
<p>Every repeated source/test/contract/artifact path has exactly one content writer. The original table below records <strong>33 base assignments: 22 I + 11 component (FL7, DT3, BE1)</strong>. The current authoritative registry retains those assignments and includes 76 unique paths (I: 62, BE: 4, FL: 7, DT: 3), including approved additive locks. For paths used entirely inside B04/B06/B07/B08/B14 without a preparatory milestone, the stable component owner continues across atomic subtasks without an intermediate I handoff. I merges the independently reviewed batch commit without separate content edits; merge conflicts return to that file owner. Source reviewers are read-only. For shared review/QA artifacts, I serializes collection of independent reviewers' results without changing their verdicts.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Exact shared path</th><th>Sole physical writer</th><th>Ordered patch/task users</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.boss/technical-review/WO-01-validation.md</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T15 -&gt; 01-T16 -&gt; 01-T17</td></tr><tr><td><code>.boss/technical-review/WO-04-validation.md</code></td><td>I</td><td>04-T13 -&gt; 04-T14 -&gt; 04-T15 -&gt; 04-T16</td></tr><tr><td><code>docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T01 -&gt; 03-T01 -&gt; 04-T01</td></tr><tr><td><code>docs/contracts/station-content-contract.md</code></td><td>I</td><td>03-T01 -&gt; 04-T01</td></tr><tr><td><code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code></td><td>I</td><td>04-T03 -&gt; 04-T09 -&gt; 04-T11 -&gt; 04-T15 -&gt; 04-T16</td></tr><tr><td><code>docs/operations/station-privacy-migration.md</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T01 -&gt; 01-T12 -&gt; 01-T16 -&gt; 01-T17</td></tr><tr><td><code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/editorial-comment-counts.test.js</code></td><td>I</td><td>04-T08 -&gt; 04-T12</td></tr><tr><td><code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/station-privacy.test.js</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T13 -&gt; 01-T14</td></tr><tr><td><code>firebase_tests/firebase-rules/firestore.rules.test.js</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T04 -&gt; 01-T11 -&gt; 03-T16 -&gt; 04-T12</td></tr><tr><td><code>firestore.indexes.json</code></td><td>I</td><td>03-T02 -&gt; 04-T12</td></tr><tr><td><code>firestore.rules</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T04 -&gt; 01-T11 -&gt; 04-T12</td></tr><tr><td><code>functions/index.js</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T09 -&gt; 03-T09 -&gt; 04-T05 -&gt; 04-T07</td></tr><tr><td><code>functions/lib/admin-content-delete.js</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T03 -&gt; 04-T07</td></tr><tr><td><code>functions/lib/stream-health.js</code></td><td>BE</td><td>04-T04 -&gt; 04-T05</td></tr><tr><td><code>lib/features/player/presentation/controllers/station_player_controller.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T02 -&gt; 02-T04</td></tr><tr><td><code>test/features/account/data/firebase_account_repository_test.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T08 -&gt; 02-T10</td></tr><tr><td><code>test/features/account/presentation/account_controller_test.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T08 -&gt; 02-T10</td></tr><tr><td><code>test/features/account/presentation/auth_screen_test.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T08 -&gt; 02-T10</td></tr><tr><td><code>test/features/account/presentation/manage_account_screen_test.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T08 -&gt; 02-T10</td></tr><tr><td><code>test/features/account/presentation/register_screen_test.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T07 -&gt; 02-T10</td></tr><tr><td><code>test/features/player/presentation/station_player_controller_test.dart</code></td><td>FL</td><td>02-T01 -&gt; 02-T03</td></tr><tr><td><code>tool/migrate_station_privacy.mjs</code></td><td>DT</td><td>01-T12 -&gt; 01-T13</td></tr><tr><td><code>tool/run-admin-emulator-tests.mjs</code></td><td>I</td><td>03-T16 -&gt; 04-T08</td></tr><tr><td><code>tool/test/migrate_station_privacy.test.mjs</code></td><td>DT</td><td>01-T12 -&gt; 01-T13</td></tr><tr><td><code>tool/test/station-writer-privacy.test.mjs</code></td><td>DT</td><td>01-T07 -&gt; 01-T08</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/components/admin/admin-app.tsx</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T06 -&gt; 01-T10 -&gt; 03-T12 -&gt; 03-T13</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/components/admin/users-aggregate-view.tsx</code></td><td>I</td><td>M03-T16-RED-READY (preparatory seam) -&gt; 03-T10 (implementation)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/lib/export-excel.ts</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T06 -&gt; 03-T13</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/lib/resource-filters.ts</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T10 -&gt; 03-T11</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/lib/user-count.ts</code></td><td>I</td><td>M03-T16-RED-READY (preparatory seam) -&gt; 03-T10 (implementation)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/test/export-excel.test.ts</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T06 -&gt; 03-T13</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/test/resource-filters.test.ts</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T10 -&gt; 03-T11</td></tr><tr><td><code>web_admin/test/save-content.emulator.test.ts</code></td><td>I</td><td>01-T05 -&gt; 01-T14</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>All <strong>33 original shared paths</strong> above remain in <code>sharedFileOwners</code> in <code>waves.json</code>; approved additive entries make the current registry total 76 unique paths. Task users describe patch handoffs, not an assertion that an entire upstream task has completed: 03-T16 contributes M03-T16-FIXTURE before 04-T08, while final 03-T16 acceptance follows 04-T08. Acquire the path lock before each write and reconcile against the latest approved artifact. The listed owner retains exclusive content-write authority; workers supply patches to I for cross-batch/control paths. New overlaps are classified and assigned one owner before dispatch; cross-batch/control overlaps belong to I. WO-02 currently does not write providers/station-content/screens/ARB; any expansion must be reconciled before B09.</p>
<h3 id="t11-canonical-helper-compatibility-attachment">T11 canonical helper compatibility attachment</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Existing shared path</th><th>Sole integration owner</th><th>Serialized task users / allowed change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>functions/lib/program-notifications.js</code></td><td>I</td><td>04-T10 -&gt; 04-T11 in B16; T11 adds only export keywords to existing pure <code>normalizedSchedule</code>, <code>localTime</code>, <code>legacyDates</code> and <code>fingerprint</code></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>This 76th ownership row preserves all 75 previous entries and all 33 original assignments. T11's explicit write set now includes this existing path so the timezone tool uses the canonical runtime normalization/date/key-fingerprint logic rather than copying it. I alone applies the reviewed source attachment under the path lock. No helper body, default, scheduler, index, task, batch, wave or dependency changes are authorized by this attachment; existing T10 -&gt; T11 ordering remains. The batch B16 and wave W04-W5 unions already contain the path. Refresh current source before patching and rerun applicable Functions/tool gates with independent review; no finding closure follows.</p>
<h2 id="3-sixteen-batches-one-assignment-per-implementation-task">3. Sixteen batches — one assignment per implementation task</h2>
<p>Listed task order does not override internal dependencies; section 3.3 specifies them. A batch write set is the union of its exact WO task write sets, with no extra files. NEW items remain proposed additions, not existing APIs.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Batch</th><th>Worker</th><th>Atomic tasks assigned exactly once</th><th>Batch predecessors</th><th>Required contracts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>B01</td><td>I</td><td>01-T01, 03-T01, 04-T01</td><td>None</td><td>Emits scoped milestones below</td></tr><tr><td>B02</td><td>BE + I</td><td>01-T02, 01-T03, 01-T04</td><td>None</td><td>C01</td></tr><tr><td>B03</td><td>WA + I</td><td>01-T05, 01-T06, 01-T10, 01-T11</td><td>B02, B05</td><td>Inherited</td></tr><tr><td>B04</td><td>DT + I</td><td>01-T07, 01-T08</td><td>B02</td><td>Inherited</td></tr><tr><td>B05</td><td>BE + I</td><td>01-T09, 01-T09a</td><td>B04</td><td>C01</td></tr><tr><td>B06</td><td>DT + I</td><td>01-T12, 01-T13</td><td>B03, B04</td><td>Inherited</td></tr><tr><td>B07</td><td>FL + I</td><td>02-T01, 02-T02, 02-T03, 02-T04</td><td>None</td><td>Existing playback contract</td></tr><tr><td>B08</td><td>FL + I</td><td>02-T05, 02-T06, 02-T07, 02-T08, 02-T09, 02-T10</td><td>None</td><td>Existing account/security contract</td></tr><tr><td>B09</td><td>FL + I</td><td>03-T03, 03-T04, 03-T05, 03-T06, 03-T07, 03-T08</td><td>B10</td><td>C03</td></tr><tr><td>B10</td><td>DT + I</td><td>03-T02</td><td>None</td><td>C03</td></tr><tr><td>B11</td><td>WA + I</td><td>03-T09, 03-T10, 03-T11, 03-T12, 03-T13</td><td>B03, B10; M03-T16-RED-READY</td><td>C03</td></tr><tr><td>B12</td><td>WP</td><td>03-T14, 03-T15</td><td>B10</td><td>C03</td></tr><tr><td>B13</td><td>BE + I</td><td>04-T02, 04-T03</td><td>B02</td><td>C04-RSS</td></tr><tr><td>B14</td><td>BE + I</td><td>04-T04, 04-T05</td><td>B11</td><td>C04-HEALTH</td></tr><tr><td>B15</td><td>BE + QA + I</td><td>04-T06, 03-T16, 04-T07, 04-T08, 04-T09, 01-T14</td><td>B06, B09, B11, B12, B13, B14</td><td>C04-COUNTS</td></tr><tr><td>B16</td><td>BE + I</td><td>04-T10, 04-T11, 04-T12, 02-T11</td><td>B07, B08, B15</td><td>C04-TIMEZONE</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3 id="3-1-scoped-contract-milestones-inside-b01">3.1 Scoped contract milestones inside B01</h3>
<p>C01 comes from reviewed 01-T01 privacy/writer decisions. C03 comes from 03-T01 after C01. Then 04-T01 emits independently reviewed <strong>C04-RSS, C04-HEALTH, C04-COUNTS and C04-TIMEZONE</strong>. I serializes shared contract edits.</p>
<p>A batch waits only for its required approved milestone, not all of B01. Unresolved R13 blocks <strong>C04-TIMEZONE/B16 only</strong>, never unrelated privacy, playback, queries or approved RSS/health/counts. Atomic task 04-T01 remains incomplete until all its outputs are approved; partial contract release is not fabricated task completion.</p>
